## test handsfree

Repo: https://github.com/FarisHijazi/claude-voice-handsfree
Local: ~/projects/claude-voice-handsfree
State dir: ~/.claude/handsfree/
Skill symlink: ~/.claude/skills/handsfree -> ~/projects/claude-voice-handsfree/plugins/handsfree/skills/handsfree

Install is DONE: Stop hook in ~/.claude/settings.json, MCP server in ~/.claude.json.

### 1. Pre-grant macOS permissions
System Settings -> Privacy & Security
  - Microphone -> grant to your terminal app
  - Speech Recognition -> grant to your terminal app
Skip this and the first dictation pops a permission dialog mid-loop.

### 2. Restart Claude Code
Quit and start a new session anywhere.

### 3. Verify MCP loaded
    /mcp        # expect "handsfree" in the list

### 4. Turn it on
    /handsfree on
Expected:
  - assistant prints short greeting
  - macOS `say` reads it aloud
  - short beep = start of listening
  - speak, say "over" to end early, OR wait
  - if no "over": beeps at 7s / 8s / 9s, cutoff beep at 10s
  - transcript -> POST /inject -> arrives in Claude as <channel source="handsfree">
  - loop continues

### 5. Debug commands (in another terminal)
    curl -s "http://127.0.0.1:$(cat ~/.claude/handsfree/port)/health"
    tail -f ~/.claude/handsfree/hook.log
    cat ~/.claude/handsfree/active && echo ON || echo OFF

    # bypass STT — inject a prompt directly to isolate TTS vs STT
    curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:$(cat ~/.claude/handsfree/port)/inject" \
      -H "authorization: Bearer $(cat ~/.claude/handsfree/token)" \
      -H "content-type: application/json" \
      -d '{"text":"what time is it?"}'

### 6. Escape hatches
    rm ~/.claude/handsfree/active   # Stop hook no-ops next turn
    Ctrl+C                          # kills listen.swift, hook skips inject
    /handsfree off

### Likely first-run failure modes
  - No TTS / no beep / no listen          -> Stop hook missing from ~/.claude/settings.json
  - /mcp does not show handsfree          -> mcpServers.handsfree missing from ~/.claude.json
  - TTS works, silent listener            -> Mic permission denied; see hook.log "not authorized"
  - Listener runs, nothing reaches Claude -> Channel not delivering; try direct /inject curl
  - Greeting plays twice / loops          -> stop_hook_active guard broken; file a bug

### Reuse findings worth remembering
  - Claude Code itself has a native `voice` config field (`voiceEnabled`,
    `voice.mode = hold|tap`, `language`) per settings.json schema (career-coach
    session bbf5533b, 21d ago). Worth checking if it works natively before
    relying on this plugin — user said skip for now.
  - ~/.claude/skills/transcribe wraps Whisper large-v3 (Arabic default) —
    fallback if SFSpeechRecognizer accuracy is poor for a language.
  - Self-hosted Whisper LXC at 192.168.50.20 (LXC 104) — local Whisper fallback.

### Files of interest
  ~/projects/claude-voice-handsfree/plugins/handsfree/server.ts
  ~/projects/claude-voice-handsfree/plugins/handsfree/scripts/stop-hook.sh
  ~/projects/claude-voice-handsfree/plugins/handsfree/scripts/listen.swift
  ~/projects/claude-voice-handsfree/plugins/handsfree/scripts/speak.sh
  ~/projects/claude-voice-handsfree/plugins/handsfree/skills/handsfree/SKILL.md
  ~/.claude/handsfree/hook.log         # Stop hook diagnostics
  ~/.claude/handsfree/{token,port}     # per-session bearer + HTTP port
  ~/.claude/handsfree/active           # flag — toggle voice mode
